    "created_at": "2024-11-14T19:46:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-14T19:46:35Z",
    "body": "> You cannot use testdriver with reftests? That seems like something that ought to be fixed if true.\r\n\r\nNot at the moment, see https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/13183. I agree we should get it fixed, and I believe work is progressing.\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\nSo we [discussed the use cases](https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1127#issuecomment-2477226488) for this capability today at OpenUI. Two concrete use cases were brought up by developers:\r\n\r\n * Opening the select picker on page load, to help the user get started with an action/choice.\r\n * \"Teaching UI\" that roams around the screen showing users how to use things, and wants to open select pickers to \"teach\" what options are available.\r\n\r\nNeither of these use cases would be possible to build without `showPicker()` that doesn't require user activation.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
